    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0701" n="679" xml:id="pg679"/>

                <head>288. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Vietnam<anchor n="1" xml:id="d288-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1961-11-28T19:37:00-05:00">November 28, 1961, 7:37
                            p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>698. State-Defense-USIA. Supersedes all previous
                    messages.</p>
                <p>Do not give other than routine cooperation to correspondents on coverage current
                    military activities in Vietnam. No comment at all on classified activities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d288-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d288-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 751K.00/11-2861. Confidential; Niact.
                    Drafted by Tubby; cleared by Tubby with Sylvester (Defense), Wilson (USIA),
                        Salinger (White House), and Heavner;
                    and signed by Tubby for the
                    Secretary.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
